openharn-myelin is the openharn agent harness (https://github.com/Thebored1/openharn,
MIT) adapted into a streaming sidecar for the Myelin desktop app.

Adapted / ported components (all MIT):
  - src/harness.rs  — openharn's reliability primitives ported verbatim in spirit
                      from openharn/src/agent.rs: cap_result, fit_context,
                      parse_text_tool_calls, flatten_for_prompt_tools, tool_grammar,
                      strip_think. Made schema-driven (works for Myelin's tool set,
                      not just openharn's coding tools).
  - src/agent.rs    — openharn's run() loop, made async + streaming (SSE) and
                      retargeted to execute tools via HTTP callbacks to the host
                      (Myelin) instead of a local tools::Session.
  - src/harness.rs::extract_partial_content / partial_field — ported from Myelin's
                      own src-tauri/src/stream_chat.rs (live write_note streaming).

openharn incorporates code and prompt text adapted from opencode
(https://github.com/sst/opencode), used under the MIT License; the opencode
license text is included at LICENSES/opencode-MIT.txt. The openharn license is at
LICENSE.openharn.
